  Slug: starless-shadow
  DisplayName: Starless Shadow
  IconPath: icons/magic/perception/eye-ringed-glow-angry-small-teal.webp
  Description: "Your patron first contacted you at the witching hour, as your body
    lay paralyzed by sleep while your mind had yet to escape the waking world. Your
    patron might be a creature of the Netherworld or a long-forgotten spirit of twilight\u2014all
    you remember of them are haunting eyes of moonlight, offering you power from
    the darkness. Spell List occult Patron Skill Occultism Lesson of Night's Terrors
    Your patron taught you that the darkness can hide all manner of things best left
    unseen. You gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Shroud of Night] hex
    cantrip, and your familiar learns @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Fear].
    Familiar of Stalking Night Your familiar is dark of fur or feather, and light
    seems to disappear into it. When you Cast or Sustain a hex, and your familiar
    is adjacent to an enemy to which it's @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Concealed],
    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Hidden], or undetected, the enemy becomes
    Frightened 1."
